 "dates": "Tuesday, September 8 – Saturday, September 12, 2009",
 "logline": "Tuesday is the Blessed Mother’s birthday, Wednesday a congressman calls the President a liar, and Thursday a boy with a guitar plays the one song he saves for once a month — and Jack walks Lena home the long way.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "Under the candles at St. Brendan’s, a small brass plate: NORA GRACE CALLOWAY · 1989–2009."
  },
  {
   "text": "Lena bought an Altoids tin in Buellton and wrote RELIQUARY on the lid. By Labor Day it held two of your cigarettes.",
   "if": "reliquary>=2"
  },
  {
   "text": "At the Getty she wrote your objection into her own paper, in her own hand, with your name after it.",
   "if": "e3_getty==\"press\""
  },
  {
   "text": "By the fire she won the argument — and you told her your father’s been laid off since June.",
   "if": "e3_told_lena_frank"
  },
  {
   "text": "Labor Day morning your brother called from Trumbull Correctional, Theo three feet away. You told Theo where Danny is. He asked one question: what does he read?",
   "if": "e3_danny_told==\"plain\""
  },
  {
   "text": "You told Nonna you’d played chess instead of going to confession. She said: go next week.",
   "if": "e3_nonna==\"truth\""
  }
 ],
